&lt;p&gt;As a Product Analyst II at HackerRank, you will own the end-to-end analytics for our products and platforms, working across AI-powered experiences, developer-facing products, content, community growth, or platform initiatives. This is not a BI reporting role — you will own and drive analytics initiatives end-to-end and act as a thought partner to Product, Engineering, Content, Design, and business stakeholders, helping answer not only &quot;what happened?&quot; but also &quot;what should we build, improve, prioritize, or measure next?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own analytics for next-generation product(s), platform, content, AI, community, or growth areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve metrics across adoption, engagement, retention, satisfaction, usability, usage quality, and customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze customer and developer journeys, segments, and feature-level behavior to identify opportunities and friction points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the quality, effectiveness, and adoption of new content and AI-powered product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Content, Design, and Marketing teams to define measurement plans and success criteria for new initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive experimentation by framing hypotheses, sizing opportunities, designing experiments, interpreting results, and recommending next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI agents as part of your daily analytics workflow, and analyze AI assistants/agentic workflows including usage, outcomes, cost, and usage-based pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3-6 years of full-time experience in product analytics, data science, growth analytics, consumer analytics, platform analytics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have advanced SQL skills and experience working with event, session, or clickstream-level product data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable using Python for analysis and working with large, imperfect, or text-based datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong foundation in statistics, including hypothesis testing, confidence intervals, statistical significance, power analysis, sampling, regression, and causal inference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand funnels, cohort analysis, segmentation, retention, experimentation, and feature adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can turn ambiguous business questions into structured analyses, clear recommendations, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Even better if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLM product metrics, AI quality evaluation, or agent workflow analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing or validating clickstream instrumentation; not only defining requirements for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience measuring content quality, learning outcomes, developer workflows, or community engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with consumer tech, developer tools, learning platforms, marketplaces, or B2B SaaS products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy owning analytics initiatives end to end, from problem framing through impact measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities evolve based on feedback and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong bias for action, experimentation, and continuous improvement in ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working across product areas and building context quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are great at collaborating with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
