&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Developer Relations (DevRel) engineer, you will be responsible for building and scaling a strong developer community around our core products. Your primary focus will be to engage developers, identify and nurture top talent, and create systems that enable the community to contribute high-quality questions at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;You will operate at the intersection of community, product, and growth, acting as both a champion for developers and a strategic partner to internal teams. This role is critical to expanding our ecosystem, increasing our talent pool in the network, and ensuring our products are shaped by real-world developer needs and expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a global network of experts to create coding challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, curate, and manage a community-sourced pipeline of high-quality hands-on questions that include problem description, canonical solutions, hints and guidelines for all our core products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nurture community participation, support developer success, and measure engagement signals to inform strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recruit and collaborate with developer champions, contributors, community leaders, and influencers to grow our reach and credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a seasoned technical community builder, and developer advocate who blends deep technical credibility with outstanding communication and relationship skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience writing code, building sample apps, or shipping technical projects that demonstrate your ability to teach by example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical foundation with experience in at least one mainstream programming language and technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. You can explain complex technical problems and solutions in ways that empower developers to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine passion for developers, deep empathy for their workflows, and a commitment to helping them succeed without resorting to sales pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Even better if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to or building for developer ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to open-source communities and technical content development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-driven workflows for scaling product capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in this role if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a builder at heart, excited to create scalable systems from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambiguity doesn’t slow you down - you bring clarity, structure, and crisp execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about developer experience, customer impact, and raising the bar in technical hiring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration energizes you, whether it’s with engineers, customers, or global experts.&lt;/li&gt;
